SQL> CREATE OR REPLACE PACKAGE otap_api
  2  AS
  3  
  4    /**
  5    * The package is fail save in the sense that it will try to capture all errors and execptions and
  6    * influence the test result. On exceptions, otap is not stable, so the test result gets undefined
  7    * exceptions and errors and the test_errors content is set. Still it is possible on severe database
  8    * errors will raise an exception. Every error passing the double begin-end blocks used are exceptions
  9    * that otap can't and won't handle. The begin-end blocks define the otap code that can be controlled,
 10    * but if database is unstable, e.g. running out of tablespace, it makes no sense to consume exceptions.
 11    *
 12    * Main functionality is to prepare the parameters considering session settings and then call the functions
 13    * to keep the basic test functions short and concentrated on their real work. The return of the test
 14    * functions should always be NUMBER, limited to otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_PASSED,
 15    * otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_FAILED, otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_UNDEFINED or exception.
 16    *
 17    * Test results, after persisting, are always delivered to the caller of OTAP_API as VARCHAR2 test result text.
 18    *
 19    * Comments are kept short, as this package gets huge. See wrapped functions for details.
 20    */
 21  
